%U A401134 24052991,48695548,97789693,189717714,383937245,769420335,1495354255,3023849838,6037121798,11931119719,24065637419,48348319846,94897165312,191581169738
%N A401134 Number of distinct equality patterns among compositions of n.
%C A401134 Two compositions (a_1,...,a_k) and (b_1,...,b_k) are equivalent if a_i = a_j if and only if b_i = b_j for all 1 <= i,j <= k.
%C A401134 The empty composition gives a(0) = 1.
%H A401134 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A401134/b401134.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..300</a>
%F A401134 a(n) = Sum_{m in M(n)} (Sum_i m_i)! / (Product_i m_i! * Product_j c_j(m)!), where M(n) is the set of distinct nonincreasing sequences obtained by sorting the multiplicities of the distinct parts of each partition of n, and c_j(m) is the number of entries of m equal to j.
%e A401134 For n = 5, the 10 equality patterns are A, AB, AAB, ABA, ABB, AAAB, AABA, ABAA, ABBB, and AAAAA. Different letters denote different part values.
%e A401134 Representatives are (5), (1,4), (1,1,3), (1,3,1), (1,2,2), (1,1,1,2), (1,1,2,1), (1,2,1,1), (2,1,1,1), and (1,1,1,1,1), respectively.
%e A401134 Using the formula, M(5) = {(1), (1,1), (2,1), (3,1), (5)}, so a(5) = 1 + 2!/(1!*1!*2!) + 3!/(2!*1!) + 4!/(3!*1!) + 1 = 10.
%Y A401134 Cf. A088314 (analogous sequence for integer partitions), A088887 (cardinality of M(n)).
%K A401134 nonn,new
%O A401134 0,3
